ReolinkLinux
============

ReolinkLinux is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or
sponsored by Reolink. "Reolink", "Duo" and "TrackMix" are trademarks of their owner and
are used only to describe compatibility.

Third-party references
----------------------

* reolink_aio (https://github.com/starkillerOG/reolink_aio), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2021 starkillerOG and contributors.
  Used as a reference for the behaviour of the Reolink HTTP API across firmware
  versions: stream URL naming, capability flags, the telephoto ("autotrack") stream of
  dual-lens cameras, and the bit layout of the event flags in recording file names
  (reolinklinux/core/recordings.py). No code is copied verbatim.

* The event-flag layout in recording file names was first documented by sven337 in the
  "Figuring out the file names" page of https://github.com/sven337/ReolinkLinux/wiki.

Runtime libraries (not bundled)
-------------------------------

* Qt / PySide6 (LGPLv3), libmpv (LGPLv2.1+ or GPLv2+ depending on the build),
  FFmpeg (LGPLv2.1+ or GPLv2+ depending on the build).
